WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.160
Welcome to our training on the brand analytics repeat purchase behavior report.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:10.260
Brands enrolled in Amazon Brand Registry enjoy access to a suite of additional

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:15.010
selling benefits including the brand analytics tool in Seller Central.

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:15.960
In this

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:20.340
video we'll review the features and functionality of one of the reports

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:22.876
you'll find in brand analytics.

00:00:22.876 --> 00:00:24.398
Repeat purchase behavior.

00:00:24.398 --> 00:00:25.920
This report helps

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.880
brands understand how frequently customers buy their products if they've

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.680
purchased them more than once.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.920
It can help them assess and respond to customer

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:39.800
engagement or they can use it to understand how satisfied customers are

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.020
with their products.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:44.680
You can access the repeat purchase behavior report and

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:49.560
others in the brand analytics tool if you're a seller internal to a brand

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.194
enrolled in brand registry.

00:00:51.194 --> 00:00:55.280
Simply select brands in the main menu in Seller Central

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:01.440
then click brand analytics or click all brand benefits then locate the brand

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:02.327
analytics card.

00:01:02.327 --> 00:01:06.760
For more information about access to brand analytics and other

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:12.160
brand registry tools see our modules in Seller University about requesting or

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:15.064
managing access to brand selling benefits.

00:01:15.064 --> 00:01:17.000
After accessing the brand

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.720
analytics tool you can select repeat purchase behavior from the list of

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.870
reports at the top of the screen.

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:26.020
The report lists each of your brands

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:30.775
according to the total number of orders received across all products.

00:01:30.775 --> 00:01:31.640
It captures

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:35.939
your sales as well as the sales of other sellers listing your products.

00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:36.600
The brand

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:41.240
with the most customer orders appears at the top with all other brands in

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.296
descending order below.

00:01:42.296 --> 00:01:46.520
In the row for each brand you'll see the total number of

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.600
orders along with a series of metrics.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:52.240
Repeat-ordered product sales are sales

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:55.324
from customers who've purchased products more than once.

00:01:55.324 --> 00:01:56.480
For example a

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:02.280
customer buys a soccer ball that's part of your brand for $10 then buys two more

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:06.480
of the same soccer balls in a separate order for $8 each.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:07.880
The repeat sales for

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:11.408
the soccer ball in this scenario would be $16.

00:02:11.408 --> 00:02:13.760
You'll see the total repeat sales

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:15.090
for each brand.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:19.080
You'll also see two related percentages change versus prior

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:21.902
period and percent share of total sales.

00:02:21.902 --> 00:02:24.320
Change versus prior period is the

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:28.720
difference in repeat sales for a brand compared to the previous reporting period.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:34.640
For example if your brand has $150 in repeat sales for the current week and

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:40.320
had $75 in repeat sales last week the difference in the change versus prior

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:45.940
period column would be 100 percent because repeat sales doubled from one

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:47.555
week to the next.

00:02:47.555 --> 00:02:52.400
Percent share of total sales is the amount in repeat sales for

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.976
a brand divided by its total sales.

00:02:54.976 --> 00:02:57.920
For example if the repeat sales for your

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:05.280
brand for the current week is $150 and total sales is $450 the percent share

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:08.660
of total sales would be 33.33 percent.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:12.040
In the next set of columns repeat

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:17.280
ordered units you'll see similar metrics with a focus on the number of units sold

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.728
rather than the amount in sales.

00:03:19.728 --> 00:03:23.400
For example if a customer buys a soccer ball

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:27.840
that's part of your brand then buys two more of the same soccer balls in a

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:32.091
separate order the number of units from repeat orders would be two.

00:03:32.091 --> 00:03:32.800
You'll see

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:36.732
the total number of units associated with repeat orders.

00:03:36.732 --> 00:03:38.480
Like with sales you'll

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:44.274
also see a change versus prior period and percent share of total units.

00:03:44.274 --> 00:03:44.720
For

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:49.200
example if the total number of units associated with repeat purchases of your

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:54.520
brand is 20 for the current week and you had 10 units associated with repeat

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:59.680
purchases last week the difference you'd see in the change versus prior period

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:05.080
column would be 100 percent because the number of units doubled from one week to

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:05.818
the next.

00:04:05.818 --> 00:04:09.880
If the number of units associated with repeat purchases of your

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:15.680
brand for the current week is 20 and the total number of units sold is 100 the

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:19.112
percent share of total sales would be 20 percent.

00:04:19.112 --> 00:04:21.400
In the next set of columns

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.800
repeat customer count you'll see similar metrics about the number of

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.825
customers who purchased your brand's products more than once.

00:04:29.825 --> 00:04:30.720
For example

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:35.720
three customers purchased your soccer ball one ordered a single soccer ball

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:41.840
one time another ordered two soccer balls then two more in a separate order and a

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:46.800
third ordered three soccer balls then two more and then four more in separate

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:47.206
orders.

00:04:47.206 --> 00:04:52.080
The total number of repeat customers in this scenario would be two

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:57.240
you'll see the total number of repeat customers for a brand along with a

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:02.560
change versus prior period which follows the same basic formula used in previous

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:04.886
columns for repeat sales and units.

00:05:04.886 --> 00:05:07.600
For example if the total number of

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:12.200
customers associated with repeat purchases of your brand is 10 for the

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:17.760
current week and you had five last week you'd see 100 percent in the change

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:22.840
versus prior period column because the number of repeat customers doubled from

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:24.602
one week to the next.

00:05:24.602 --> 00:05:28.480
In the last set of columns repeat customer share you'll see

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:33.840
two additional percentages percent share of total customers is the number of

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:39.000
repeat customers for the brand listed in the previous column divided by the number

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:44.400
of unique customers for the brand and change versus prior period is the

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:48.480
difference in the percentage of repeat customers compared to the previous

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:49.440
reporting period.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:53.760
For example if the number of customers associated with

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:58.920
repeat purchases of your brand is 10 for the current week and the total number of

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:05.760
unique customers is 40 the percent share of total customers would be 25% if the

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:10.280
percent share of total customers last week had been 20 percent the change

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:13.188
versus prior period would be five percent.

00:06:13.188 --> 00:06:15.680
When you first access the repeat

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:20.400
purchase behavior report it'll be defaulted to show metrics for each of your

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:21.975
brands for the previous week.

00:06:21.975 --> 00:06:25.440
You can click ASIN view at the top of the

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:28.667
report to view the same metrics at the product level.

00:06:28.667 --> 00:06:30.280
Use this view to better

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:32.791
understand repeat purchases within a brand.

00:06:32.791 --> 00:06:35.720
Back on the brand View section of

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:40.560
the report you can use the drop-down menus at the top to view a specific time

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:40.986
period.

00:06:40.986 --> 00:06:46.520
When doing so keep in mind that data is generally available in brand

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:48.387
analytics within 72 hours.

00:06:48.387 --> 00:06:52.120
After selecting a time period click the apply

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:53.808
button to refresh the report.

00:06:53.808 --> 00:06:57.520
You can also use filters to narrow the report to a

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:58.349
specific brand.

00:06:58.349 --> 00:07:03.320
Click show filters then use the drop-down menu to select a

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:03.728
brand.

00:07:03.728 --> 00:07:07.400
Click the refine results button to refresh the report.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.440
If you'd like to add

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:14.800
or remove columns on the repeat purchase behavior report click customize columns

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:19.910
on the right hand side then check or uncheck boxes in the pop-up.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:20.640
Click the

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:23.755
save button to return to the updated report.

00:07:23.755 --> 00:07:26.480
To download a copy of the report

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:32.000
click the generate download button then in the pop-up select either simple view

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:37.160
to download the report you see on screen or select comprehensive view to

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:40.291
download the report with all relevant columns.

00:07:40.291 --> 00:07:42.080
Click the generate download

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:46.540
button to start your download which you can monitor by accessing the download

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:46.948
manager.

00:07:46.948 --> 00:07:51.440
Finally if you want more information about how a specific metric

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:56.800
is calculated click metrics glossary to see a set of comprehensive definitions.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:02.320
On the metrics glossary page you can expand each section to see additional

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:02.735
details.

00:08:02.735 --> 00:08:07.720
We encourage brands to use all the features and functionality of the

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:12.520
repeat purchase behavior report to get insights into their performance in the

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:13.440
Amazon store.

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:18.040
Use it to understand customer engagement for your brand how

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:23.200
often customers re-engage with products or use repeat purchases to gauge

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:28.700
customer satisfaction what they buy enjoy and decide to buy again.

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:29.200
This

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:32.590
concludes our overview of the repeat purchase behavior report.

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:33.720
If you'd like

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:39.160
step-by-step instructions for other brand analytics reports see our series of

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:41.609
modules in Seller University.

00:08:41.609 --> 00:08:46.633
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store.
